WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.055
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.055 --> 00:00:03.600
Cooking is about using
your senses and intuition.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.850
You don't need measuring cups.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:05.975
This is your measuring cup.

00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:06.880
One cup, two cup.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.826
[LAUGHS]

00:00:07.826 --> 00:00:10.550
I'm a Korean-American
LA kid, immigrant kid,

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.710
but the food that I cook
is American, you know?

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.210
I was raised here.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.940
There are a lot of things that I
won't teach you in this class--

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.720
exact measurements, exact
volume, precise cuts.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.160
I really believe in wiggle room.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:22.760
[LAUGHS]

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.170
I like to wiggle.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.262
We had this truck,
we had Twitter,

00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:28.220
and it was an opportunity
to just cook the food

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.210
that we wanted to cook.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.293
We didn't know it was going
to start a revolution.

00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:33.410
Told you I'm not going to
show you the kogi taco,

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.690
but I'm actually showing
you the kogi taco.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.634
[BLEEP]

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.898
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:38.898 --> 00:00:40.440
In this class, I'm
going to teach you

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.970
how to make my mother sauces--

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.670
kimchi, panchan, the
kimchi tuna melt,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.655
carnitas, mung bean
potato scallion pancakes.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.800
If you don't look like Dexter
by the time you finish making

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.660
kimchi, you didn't do it right.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.360
A lot of times you'll see in
recipes, use only the leaves.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.800
Discard the stems.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.090
Erase all that bullshit
from your mind.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.730
Use the whole vegetable.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.470
What's the worst
that could happen?

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.880
It's going to taste better?

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.260
Yeah.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.600
Now this is what you
came to MasterClass for.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.380
Look at this.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.020
Growing up as a young
kid here in Los Angeles,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.420
it was very tough
Monday through Friday

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.830
for a lot of immigrant families.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.560
We were made fun of and bullied.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.260
We had to just do whatever
we had to do to survive.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.690
But the weekends were for us.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.090
The weekends are when we
used to go to the park

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.930
and everyone would bring kalbi
and short rib to the party.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.150
And I swear, when you
put this on the grill,

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.920
you can't stop
people from eating it

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.420
before it hits the table.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.780
I want to teach you a lot
about instinct, about feel,

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.960
about seeing things, hearing
things, smelling things.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.760
To me, that's really cooking.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.770
You didn't learn how
to make a recipe.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:48.970
You learned how to cook.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.480
It will live with you forever.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.450
I will live with you
forever and you'll never

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.320
be able to get rid of me.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.365
I'm Roy Choi, and
this is MasterClass.

00:01:56.365 --> 00:02:01.032
[MUSIC PLAYING]

